# STATION 6: heal, stat, effect, cure, and reading stats.
npc: @test_body
title: Station 6 - Body
speaker: Tester

== start
TEST 6: Body. Your health is {stat("Health")} of {max_stat("Health")}. Take some fall damage first for a useful test.
-> Heal fully (expect health back to max and a "You feel better" line)
    <<heal>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Set health to 10 (expect your health bar to drop)
    <<stat Health 10>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Add 5 health (expect +5)
    <<stat Health +5>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Apply regeneration buff (expect a buff icon; effect("HealthRegen_Buff_T1") becomes true)
    <<effect HealthRegen_Buff_T1>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Do I have the regen buff? (expect yes right after applying it)
    <<if effect("HealthRegen_Buff_T1")>>
      Yes, the regeneration buff is active.
    <<else>>
      No buff active.
    <<endif>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Cure the regen buff (expect the icon to disappear)
    <<cure HealthRegen_Buff_T1>>
    <<jump start>>
-> Leave
    <<end>>
